FUN_1000_38cc (frame/vsync wait): CF-driven spin folded to an infinite loop.

asm 0x138cc: `xor al,al; xchg al,[0x3e00]` (save+clear the frame semaphore into al), then
`L: lcall far [DGROUP:0x40a]; jae L` (spin while the vsync/frame poll FUN_1000_35a7 returns CF=0), then
`[0x3e00]=al` (restore).  Ghidra dropped the x86 CF and folded the loop to `while(!(bool)uVar2)` with uVar2
a hardcoded 0 -> the frame-wait never terminates (the intro-animation player FUN_0000_e584 hangs before its
first frame).  Thread the poll's CF via the shim global g_fist_cf (set by the reconstructed FUN_1000_35a7,
patch 073); loop until CF==1.  DAT_1000_fe00 == DGROUP:0x3e00, so the save/clear/restore is already faithful.
